Askew's point is proven: the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">national</span> <span style="color: #3E88B3;">opposition</span> is not sincere in their intentions of entering government and governing responsibly. 

Perhaps an agreement can still be reached, but time is running out before the Assembly reconvenes. The immediate fallout from the collapse in negotiations has led many <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> protest voters and disillusioned conservatives to abandon ship, convinced that the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> is incapable of actually governing.